            <ArticleTitle>[The pharmacodynamics of proxodolol when administered once and in a course of doses to patients with stenocardia of effort].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>54-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effects of placebo and proxodolol, a new hybrid (beta-, alpha-) adrenoblocking agent, on exercise tolerance, hemodynamics and the conduction system were compared in 28 patients with coronary heart disease, Functional Class II-III exercise-induced angina pectoris at rest and during bicycle ergometric exercise test. Proxodolol was shown to exert a significant dose-dependent antianginal effect without producing any negative effect on atrioventricular and intraventricular conduction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
